# Two LANs Connected by Router

## 🎯 Objective

Connect two different LANs using a router and test communication between them.

## 🖥️ Devices

* 2 PCs
* 2 Cisco 2960 Switches
* 1 Cisco Router

## 🌐 IP Addressing

| Device      | IP Address     | Subnet Mask     | Gateway       |
| ----------- | -------------- | --------------- | ------------- |
| PC0         | `192.168.1.10` | `255.255.255.0` | `192.168.1.1` |
| Router G0/0 | `192.168.1.1`  | `255.255.255.0` | —             |
| Router G0/1 | `192.168.2.1`  | `255.255.255.0` | —             |
| PC1         | `192.168.2.10` | `255.255.255.0` | `192.168.2.1` |

## 🔧 Configuration

The router was configured with two interfaces to connect the two different networks.

* LAN 1: `192.168.1.0/24`
* LAN 2: `192.168.2.0/24`

## 🧪 Testing

Ping was used to test communication between PC0 and PC1.

## ✅ Result

Successfully established communication between two different LANs through the router.

## 📚 What I Learned

* How routers connect different networks
* Default gateway configuration
* Basic IP addressing
* Testing network connectivity using `ping`
